---
import:
  - undying-tide-base
requires:
  - depths
exported_concepts: [":CombJelly:", ":AnchovySchool:", ":ArrowWorm:", ":StingingJelly:", ":FlickerJelly:", ":SplitJelly:", ":Polyp:", ":Sunfish:", ":Upgrade:", ":UpgradeChoice:"]
description: Predators - the Drift-corrupted predators, hearts, the sting, the dash and the jellyfish's upgrades.
---

***definitions***

- :CombJelly: is a glowing comb jelly :Predator:, a circle of radius 20, that slowly follows the :Jellyfish:.

- :AnchovySchool: is a :Predator: made of 8 anchovies, each a circle of radius 8, swimming together in a band across the :Level:.

- :ArrowWorm: is a :Predator:, a circle of radius 14, that lies in wait and lunges at the :Jellyfish:.

- :StingingJelly: is a larger jellyfish :Predator: with a bell, a circle of radius 36, and 4 trailing tentacle segments, each a circle of radius 10.

- :FlickerJelly: is a :CombJelly: twisted by the Drift that blinks out of the :Level: and back in.

- :SplitJelly: is a :CombJelly: swollen by the Drift, a circle of radius 26, that splits in two when stung.

- :Polyp: is the stage the :Jellyfish: turns into on losing its last heart, rooted where it stands until it regenerates; its circle stays radius 24.

- :Sunfish: is a huge ocean sunfish :Predator:, a circle of radius 70, that eats the :Jellyfish:.

- :Upgrade: is a lasting improvement of the :Jellyfish: for the rest of a :Run:, one of seven kinds, each with an `id`: Stinging tentacles (`stingingTentacles`), Extra heart (`extraHeart`), Quick regeneration (`quickRegeneration`), Hard bell (`hardBell`), Wide sting (`wideSting`), Fragment magnet (`fragmentMagnet`) and Longer tentacles (`longerTentacles`).
  - A :Run: starts with no :Upgrade:.
  - Stinging tentacles can be taken once; every other kind has levels 1 to 3, one more each time it is taken.

- :UpgradeChoice: is the screen shown over the :Level: of :DivePage: between entering an open :Rift: and the start of the next :Level:, on which the player takes one :Upgrade:.

- :TentacleReach: is the circle the :Jellyfish: tentacles touch with, radius 30, its centre 50 px from the :Jellyfish: centre: straight behind it, opposite its :Heading:, at rest, turned towards the direction opposite the :Jellyfish: velocity by `min(1, <speed> / 240)` of the angle between the two.
  - It is worked out from the simulation state alone, never from the drawn tentacles.

***implementation reqs***

- :Implementation: draws the offers of an :UpgradeChoice: from a generator of `src/game/sim/random.ts` seeded from the :RunSeed: and the :Depth: of the :Rift: entered, apart from the one the :Level: layouts are drawn from, so taking an :Upgrade: changes no other draw of the :Run:.

***functional specs***

- Each :Level: holds `1 + floor((:Depth: - 1) / 2)` :CombJelly: items, each swimming straight towards the :Jellyfish: centre at `50 × :PredatorPace:` px/s.
  - A :CombJelly: never leaves the :Level:.
  - A :CombJelly: stands still while the :Run: is paused and after the :RunEnd:.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `predators`, the list of every :Predator: in the :Level:, each with `id` (unique in the :Run:), `kind` (`combJelly` here), `x`, `y` and `radius`.
  - The same :RunSeed: gives each :Depth: the same :Predator: starts.

- A :Predator: touching the :Jellyfish: takes one of its :Hearts:, and 2 s of :Invulnerability: follow, in which the :Jellyfish: blinks.
  - A :Predator: touches the :Jellyfish: when their circles overlap.
  - When several :Predator: items start touching the :Jellyfish: in the same moment, only one of its :Hearts: is taken.
  - When :Hearts: reaches 0 the :Jellyfish: becomes a :Polyp:; losing hearts never brings the :RunEnd:.
  - :Hearts: carry over from one :Level: to the next, and the time left of an :Invulnerability: does too.
  - The :Invulnerability: clock does not run while the :Run: is paused.
  - The :Predator: that touches the :Jellyfish: keeps swimming as before, and the :Jellyfish: can swim during the :Invulnerability:.
  - A :Predator: touching the :Jellyfish: during an :Invulnerability: takes nothing; one still touching it when the :Invulnerability: ends takes another of its :Hearts:, each time one ends.
  - :Hud: shows one heart in the palette's heart colour for each of the :Hearts:.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `hearts` and `invulnerableFor` (seconds left, 0 when none).

- Space fires the :Sting:, which costs 3 :Pulses: and purifies every :Predator: whose circle it reaches; a purified :Predator: leaves the :Level:.
  - The :Sting: reaches a :Predator: when the distance between their centres is at most `90 + ` the :Predator: radius.
  - After a :Sting:, Space does nothing for 1 s; holding Space does not fire again.
  - Each press of Space fires at most one :Sting:, on the update right after it or not at all; a press that cannot fire then is dropped, never kept for later.
  - Space does nothing while :Pulses: is 3 or less.
  - A :Sting: is drawn as a ring in the palette's sting colour, widening to 90 px over 1 s and fading out over its last 0.2 s; the ring is only drawn, and the :Sting: still purifies at the moment it is fired.
  - Space does nothing while the :Run: is paused or after the :RunEnd:.
  - :Hud: shows `Purified <n>`, the :Predator: items purified in the :Run: so far.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `purified` (the count for the :Run:) and `stingCooldown` (seconds left, 0 when ready).

- Shift starts a :Dash:: for 0.25 s the :Jellyfish: swims at 720 px/s, and it has :Invulnerability: for as long.
  - The :Dash: goes forward along the :Jellyfish: :Heading: while Arrow Up or W is held, backward while Arrow Down or S is held, else in the direction the :Jellyfish: is moving.
  - Shift does nothing when neither Up nor Down is held and the :Jellyfish: is at rest.
  - A :Dash: costs no :Pulses:, which run down at the swimming rate of 1 a second while it lasts.
  - Shift does nothing for 2 s after a :Dash: starts; holding Shift does not dash again.
  - A :Dash: ends early at an edge of the :Level:, and the :Jellyfish: leaves it at its top speed of 280 px/s.
  - A :Dash: does not lengthen nor shorten an :Invulnerability: that was already running.
  - The :Jellyfish: does not blink for the :Invulnerability: of a :Dash:; it blinks during a :Dash: only while the :Invulnerability: that follows a hit is running.
  - :Hud: shows the :Dash: as ready, or as a filling ring while it waits.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `dashing` (boolean) and `dashCooldown` (seconds left, 0 when ready).

- A :Jellyfish: that loses its last heart is a :Polyp: for 3 s where it stands, then turns back into the :Jellyfish: there with its :Hearts: at 3 and its :Pulses: refilled to their start for the :Level:.
  - It turns back upright, its :Heading: 0, whatever its :Heading: was.
  - Its speed drops to 0 at once, and it does not move while a :Polyp:; direction keys, Shift and Space do nothing.
  - :Pulses: does not run down while it is a :Polyp:.
  - A :Jellyfish: whose :Pulses: reaches 0 becomes a :Polyp: in the same way; it turns back just as after losing its last heart, its :Hearts: at 3 and its :Pulses: refilled to their start for the :Level:.
  - :Hud: shows `Out of pulses - regenerating` in place of `Regenerating` for a :Polyp: that came from running out of :Pulses:.
  - A :Polyp: touching an open :Rift: enters it, as the :Jellyfish: does.
  - It has :Invulnerability: for the 3 s, in place of the 2 s that follow a hit, and does not blink.
  - The 3 s do not run while the :Run: is paused.
  - It is drawn as the polyp figure in place of the :Jellyfish: figure.
  - :Hud: shows `Regenerating` while it is a :Polyp:.
  - It can become a :Polyp: any number of times in a :Run:.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `polyp` (boolean) and `polypFor` (seconds left, 0 when not a :Polyp:).
  - While it is a :Polyp:, no :Predator: chases it: every :Predator: that swims towards the :Jellyfish: wanders instead, at its own speed, towards a point in the :Level: it picks from the :RunSeed:, picking a new one on reaching it or every 4 s, and swims towards the :Jellyfish: again once the :Polyp: turns back.

- From :Depth: 2, each :Level: holds `1 + floor((:Depth: - 2) / 3)` :AnchovySchool: items, each sweeping straight across the :Level: from one edge to the opposite one at `260 × :PredatorPace:` px/s.
  - An :AnchovySchool: enters from outside an edge, chosen with its row or column from the :RunSeed:, and sweeps again from a new edge 3 s after it has wholly left.
  - The :AnchovySchool: is placed off-screen at the start of the :Level:, the 250 px rule aside, and enters after 2 s.
  - Any of its anchovies touching the :Jellyfish: counts as the :AnchovySchool: touching it.
  - The :Sting: reaching any of its anchovies purifies the whole :AnchovySchool:.
  - It stands still while the :Run: is paused and after the :RunEnd:.
  - In :StateSnapshot:, its `kind` is `anchovySchool`, `x`, `y` are its centre, `radius` is 40, and it adds `fish`, the list of `x`, `y` of each anchovy.

- Each :Level: holds `1 + floor((:Depth: - 1) / 3)` :ArrowWorm: items, each lying still until the :Jellyfish: centre comes within 220 px of it, then lunging at it.
  - A lunge starts 0.4 s later, aimed at where the :Jellyfish: centre was when the 0.4 s began, and goes straight at `600 × :PredatorPace:` px/s for 0.5 s or until an edge.
  - After a lunge the :ArrowWorm: rests 1.5 s where it stopped, then lies in wait again; when the :Jellyfish: centre is within 220 px as the rest ends, the next lunge's 0.4 s begin at once.
  - It quivers while it gets ready to lunge.
  - It starts no new 0.4 s of aiming while the :Jellyfish: is a :Polyp:; a lunge already aimed goes on.
  - It stands still while the :Run: is paused and after the :RunEnd:; its timers do too.
  - In :StateSnapshot:, its `kind` is `arrowWorm`, and it adds `phase`: `waiting`, `aiming`, `lunging` or `resting`.

- From :Depth: 3, each :Level: holds `1 + floor((:Depth: - 3) / 4)` :StingingJelly: items, each drifting at `30 × :PredatorPace:` px/s towards a point in the :Level: it picks from the :RunSeed:, picking a new one on reaching it or every 4 s.
  - Its tentacle segments trail behind the bell, against its direction of travel, 30 px apart, the first 30 px from the edge of the bell.
  - Each tentacle segment is drawn with a tentacle-segment figure of its own, not the bell's.
  - The bell or any tentacle segment touching the :Jellyfish: counts as the :StingingJelly: touching it.
  - Only the :Sting: reaching its bell purifies a :StingingJelly:; reaching only its tentacles does nothing.
  - Its bell never leaves the :Level:.
  - It stands still while the :Run: is paused and after the :RunEnd:.
  - In :StateSnapshot:, its `kind` is `stingingJelly`, `x`, `y` and `radius` are its bell, and it adds `tentacles`, the list of `x`, `y` of each segment.

- From :Depth: 4, each :Level: holds `1 + floor((:Depth: - 4) / 3)` :FlickerJelly: items besides its :CombJelly: items, each following the :Jellyfish: as a :CombJelly: does, but out of the :Level: for 1 s of every 3 s.
  - Its first 3 s start with 2 s in the :Level:, then 1 s out; its 3 s cycle stands still while the :Run: is paused.
  - While out, it is not drawn, cannot touch the :Jellyfish:, cannot be reached by the :Sting:, and does not move.
  - In its last 0.3 s before going out a flickering disc in the palette's drift-flicker colour is drawn over its figure.
  - Its pace is the :CombJelly: pace.
  - In :StateSnapshot:, its `kind` is `flickerJelly`, and it adds `present` (boolean).

- From :Depth: 5, each :Level: holds `1 + floor((:Depth: - 5) / 3)` :SplitJelly: items, each following the :Jellyfish: as a :CombJelly: does; the :Sting: reaching a :SplitJelly: splits it into two :CombJelly: items instead of purifying it.
  - The two :CombJelly: items appear 30 px to either side of its centre, across the line to the :Jellyfish:, and swim at `65 × :PredatorPace:` px/s.
  - Each of the two is a :Predator: of its own from the moment it appears: one touching the :Jellyfish: outside an :Invulnerability: takes one of its :Hearts:, even if the :SplitJelly: was touching it.
  - The :Sting: that splits a :SplitJelly: does not reach the two :CombJelly: items it splits into.
  - Splitting is not purifying: `purified` does not grow for it; purifying each :CombJelly: after does.
  - The two :CombJelly: items stay within the :Level:.
  - In :StateSnapshot:, its `kind` is `splitJelly`; the two it splits into are `combJelly`, each with a new `id`.

- From :Depth: 4, each :Level: holds one :Sunfish: with a chance of 25%, drawn from the :RunSeed:; it swims straight towards the :Jellyfish: centre at `40 × :PredatorPace:` px/s, and touching the :Jellyfish: eats it.
  - The same :RunSeed: gives each :Depth: the same :Sunfish: or none.
  - Being eaten brings the :RunEnd: at once, with the reason `eaten`, whatever the :Hearts: of the :Jellyfish:, during an :Invulnerability: and while it is a :Polyp: too.
  - Being eaten takes none of the :Hearts:.
  - At the :RunEnd: with the reason `eaten`, :DivePage: shows the heading `Eaten by a sunfish` and below it `It swallowed you at depth <n>. A sting stuns a sunfish for 1.5 s.`
  - A :Sunfish: wanders while the :Jellyfish: is a :Polyp:, as a chasing :Predator: does, and still eats the :Polyp: on touching it.
  - The :Sting: reaching a :Sunfish: does not purify it; it stops for 1.5 s, then swims towards the :Jellyfish: again, and `purified` does not grow.
  - The 1.5 s do not run while the :Run: is paused.
  - Its whole circle stays within the :Level:, from its start on.
  - It stands still while the :Run: is paused and after the :RunEnd:.
  - In :StateSnapshot:, its `kind` is `sunfish`.

- Entering an open :Rift: shows the :UpgradeChoice: before the next :Level: starts: the heading `Choose an upgrade` and 3 different :Upgrade: kinds drawn from the :RunSeed:, each a button with its name, the first with the focus.
  - Only kinds that can still be taken are offered; with fewer than 3 left, all of them are, and with none left, the next :Level: starts at once with no :UpgradeChoice:.
  - Below the heading it shows `Depth <n> cleared`, the :Depth: of the :Rift: entered.
  - The buttons stand side by side, each showing, under its name, the level it brings - `Level <n> of 3`, or `Once` for Stinging tentacles - and the line of what it gives:
    - Stinging tentacles: `Tentacles purify predators they touch`.
    - Extra heart: `Up to <n> hearts (was <m>)`.
    - Quick regeneration: `Polyp stage <t> s (was <t0> s)`.
    - Hard bell: `<t> s invulnerable after a hit (was <t0> s)`.
    - Wide sting: `Sting reaches <r> px (was <r0> px)`.
    - Fragment magnet: `Pulls fragments within <r> px` at level 1, `Pulls fragments within <r> px (was <r0> px)` after.
    - Longer tentacles: `Tentacles reach <r> px (was <r0> px)`, where the reach is the :TentacleReach: centre distance plus its radius.
  - Arrow Left, Arrow Right, Arrow Up and Arrow Down, and A, D, W and S, move the focus between the buttons; Enter or Space on one takes that :Upgrade: and starts the next :Level:.
  - While it is shown, `tick`, every position, timer and :Pulses: stand still as when paused, `paused` stays false, and P and Escape do nothing.
  - Direction keys, Shift and Space held when it closes count as released.
  - The same :RunSeed: and the same :Upgrade: items taken give the same offers at every :UpgradeChoice:.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `upgradeChoice`, the list of the `id` of each :Upgrade: offered, `null` while no :UpgradeChoice: is shown, and `upgrades`, an object giving for every :Upgrade: `id` the times it has been taken in the :Run:, 0 when never.

- Each level of Extra heart raises the most :Hearts: the :Jellyfish: can have by 1, from 3 to at most 6, and adds 1 to its :Hearts: when taken.
  - A :Polyp: turns back with its :Hearts: at that most, `3 +` the Extra heart level, whether it lost its last heart or ran out of :Pulses:.
  - :Hud: shows one heart for each of the :Hearts:, up to 6.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `maxHearts`.

- Each level of Quick regeneration shortens the :Polyp: stage by 0.6 s, from 3 s to 2.4, 1.8 and 1.2 s, and its :Invulnerability: with it.
  - A :Polyp: stage already running when it is taken keeps its time left.

- Each level of Hard bell lengthens the :Invulnerability: that follows a hit by 0.75 s, from 2 s to 2.75, 3.5 and 4.25 s, the :Jellyfish: blinking throughout.
  - It does not lengthen the :Invulnerability: of a :Dash: or of a :Polyp:.

- Each level of Wide sting lengthens the reach of the :Sting: by 25 px, from 90 px to 115, 140 and 165 px.
  - The :Sting: reaches a :Predator: when the distance between their centres is at most the reach plus the :Predator: radius.
  - Its ring widens to the reach over the same 1 s.

- With Fragment magnet, every :GeneFragment: not yet collected whose centre is within 120, 180 or 240 px of the :Jellyfish: centre, at level 1, 2 or 3, moves straight towards that centre at 150 px/s.
  - One further away stays where it is, and stays where it stopped once out of range again.
  - It moves while the :Jellyfish: is a :Polyp: too, and stands still while the :Run: is paused or on an :UpgradeChoice:.
  - The `x`, `y` of each :GeneFragment: in :StateSnapshot: follow it.

- With Stinging tentacles, a :Predator: other than a :Sunfish: whose circle overlaps the :TentacleReach: is purified, as by the :Sting:, and takes none of the :Hearts:, even when it touches the :Jellyfish: circle in the same moment.
  - For a :StingingJelly: only its bell counts; its tentacle segments overlapping the :TentacleReach: purify nothing.
  - Any anchovy overlapping it purifies the whole :AnchovySchool:; a :FlickerJelly: counts only while in the :Level:.
  - A :SplitJelly: splits instead, as when stung; the two :CombJelly: items it splits into can be purified by it from the next update.
  - It purifies during an :Invulnerability: too, and not while the :Jellyfish: is a :Polyp:.
  - :StateSnapshot: adds `tentacleReach`, with `x`, `y` and `radius`.

- Each level of Longer tentacles moves the :TentacleReach: centre 15 px further from the :Jellyfish: centre and grows its radius by 5 px: from 50 px and 30 px to 65 and 35, 80 and 40, and 95 and 45 px, so it reaches 80, 100, 120 and 140 px out.
  - It turns with the :Jellyfish: velocity as before; only its distance and radius change.
  - `tentacleReach` in :StateSnapshot: follows it.
  - It is offered and can be taken before Stinging tentacles; its levels change the :TentacleReach: at once, and purify only once Stinging tentacles is taken too.

- No :GeneFragment:, :PlanktonCloud:, :Rift: or :Predator: is placed with any part of its circle inside the rectangle from `(0, 0)` to `(300, 290)` of the :Level:, the area :Hud: covers.
  - For a :StingingJelly: this holds for its bell and every tentacle segment; an :AnchovySchool:, placed off-screen, swims in as before.
  - Once placed, a :Predator: or a moving :GeneFragment: may move into the rectangle, as may the :Jellyfish:.
  - Every other placement rule still holds, and the same :RunSeed: still gives the same placements.

- A pushing :Wave: pushes every :Predator: whose circle overlaps it along its direction at its push, on top of the :Predator:'s own movement, as it pushes the :Jellyfish:.
  - A :StingingJelly: is pushed when its bell overlaps the :Wave:, its tentacle segments trailing as before; an :AnchovySchool: is pushed whole when any anchovy overlaps it.
  - A :FlickerJelly: out of the :Level: is not pushed.
  - Every rule that keeps a :Predator: within the :Level: still holds; an :AnchovySchool: pushed out of the :Level: counts as having wholly left it.
  - The push does not change where a :Predator: aims or heads: an :ArrowWorm:'s aimed point and a wanderer's picked point stay as they were.
  - The :Jellyfish: is pushed during a :Dash: too; a :Polyp: is not moved.
  - A :Wave: and its timers stand still while an :UpgradeChoice: is shown.
